8avz|n|An incrustation over a sore, wound, vesicle, or pustule, formed by the drying up of the discharge from the diseased part. ; The itch in man; also, the scurvy. ; The mange, esp. when it appears on sheep. ; A disease of potatoes producing pits in their surface, caused by a minute fungus (Tiburcinia Scabies). ; A slight irregular protuberance which defaces the surface of a casting, caused by the breaking away of a part of the mold. ; A mean, dirty, paltry fellow. ; A nickname for a workman who engages for lower wages than are fixed by the trades unions; also, for one who takes the place of a workman on a strike.	a:56sm,76,1;2o4c,57,2~2o4c,57,2;56sm,76,1	V:52v9,77,1;1bsr,63,10;6kqv,6,1~1bsr,63,10;6kqv,6,1;52v9,77,1	n:gp8,85,48;56sm,76,1~gp8,85,48;56sm,76,1	N:1bsr,53,5;am6c,45,1;6kqv,16,2~1bsr,53,5;6kqv,16,2;am6c,45,1
