8az1|v|To weigh or measure according to a scale; to measure; also, to grade or vary according to a scale or system. ; To strip or clear of scale or scales; as, to scale a fish; to scale the inside of a boiler. ; To take off in thin layers or scales, as tartar from the teeth; to pare off, as a surface. ; To scatter; to spread. ; To clean, as the inside of a cannon, by the explosion of a small quantity of powder. ; To separate and come off in thin layers or laminae; as, some sandstone scales by exposure. ; To separate; to scatter. ; To climb by a ladder, or as if by a ladder; to ascend by steps or by climbing; to clamber up; as, to scale the wall of a fort. ; To lead up by steps; to ascend.	o:9asz,28,7;6sai,26,16;7hcx,23,4;a5oj,22,50;2n29,20,9;4lty,18,28;2q0o,17,2;yh7,16,17;1rw,13,2;2tff,12,2;6obc,12,5;2mj9,11,12;1ntn,10,2;95ef,9,9;7hcu,8,4~31nq,0,526;a5oj,22,50;a7v5,2,32;4lty,18,28;yh7,16,17;6sai,26,16;2mj9,11,12;8yjy,0,10;95ef,9,9;2n29,20,9;9asz,28,7;6obc,12,5;7hcx,23,4;7hcu,8,4;5sox,6,3	s:100v,68,409;9n5b,62,32;2jfl,60,11;apz4,50,11;9vha,39,2;53zy,38,2;asat,38,3;19fo,29,10;98zd,19,5;1ejn,19,8;12dt,17,4;5sox,13,5;2wbl,13,42;dq0,12,5;2p1n,11,6~100v,68,409;2wbl,13,42;9n5b,62,32;apz4,50,11;2jfl,60,11;6q6q,4,11;19fo,29,10;115m,6,9;1ejn,19,8;2p1n,11,6;9n1b,9,6;dq0,12,5;98zd,19,5;5sox,13,5;12dt,17,4	d:2suk,53,15;7zhd,48,7;7hcv,44,56;417,37,3;45k7,35,174;7hcz,25,3;4jx1,20,7;oaz,19,949;5lfv,18,20;5d02,16,2;3tqd,15,35;8duo,14,8;2qfd,11,603;hb2,9,32;2fx0,8,5~oaz,19,949;2qfd,11,603;45k7,35,174;2puv,5,134;7hcv,44,56;3tqd,15,35;hb2,9,32;5lfv,18,20;abgn,0,19;2suk,53,15;8sjh,3,15;3tmf,5,8;8duo,14,8;4jx1,20,7;7zhd,48,7	D:59ft,78,3;7hcz,69,66;7hcv,68,301;20if,68,15;7mdz,61,57;7zhd,60,16;5d02,54,28;45k7,52,588;59mb,41,655;3d52,40,4;795f,38,16;248,37,328;33w2,36,112;4lxe,34,36;abgn,34,192~aiae,16,3550;59mb,41,655;45k7,52,588;7h2o,12,451;248,37,328;7hcv,68,301;6bnw,29,262;oaz,0,254;abgn,34,192;2fn3,16,173;hb2,32,154;79kf,23,116;33w2,36,112;qqw,23,101;4fdk,19,98
